 # External GPT Project Review
 
+## Current policy: optional only (2026-09-09)
+
+The user retired mandatory external review because the specification changed.
+External review is NOT an implementation, deployment, simulator, or M4 gate.
+Do not enqueue, claim, send, poll or automatically retry reviews unless the user
+explicitly requests external review for the current task. A pending/busy queue
+does not block ordinary work. Review queue workflow_advance_allowed describes
+the historical review workflow only, not present runtime authorization.
+
+Local code review, focused tests, source/install/config verification, stopping
+and authority checks, explicit live scope and finite budgets still apply.
+No physical safety check, test failure or motion authorization is waived.
+No old request/result/claim/lease is deleted or marked approved by this change.
+Unsent legacy requests must not be submitted automatically; an explicitly
+requested future review must confirm current source and user scope first.
+
+## Historical procedures below (inactive; not normative requirements)
+
+Everything below is retained to preserve existing edits and historical evidence.
+Its mandatory wording, gate rules, automatic transport/delegation, retries and
+deferrals do not apply to current tasks. If a user requests external review,
+agree its scope explicitly; retain record integrity and never steal another
+transport's lease. This section does not reactivate historical mandatory gates.
+
 Read this document before a non-trivial robotics/autonomous-driving change, any
 external GPT review operation, or an M4 acceptance transition.
 
